WEBVTT

00:00:07.308 --> 00:00:08.222
Excuse me, sir.

00:00:08.265 --> 00:00:09.919
Where's
Professor Lupin?

00:00:09.963 --> 00:00:13.575
That's not really your concern,
is it, Potter?

00:00:13.618 --> 00:00:17.187
Suffice it to say that
your professor finds himself

00:00:17.231 --> 00:00:20.582
incapable of teaching
at the present time.

00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:25.021
Turn to page 394.

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:30.461
"Werewolves?"

00:00:30.505 --> 00:00:32.072
But, sir, we've just
begun learning

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:33.900
about Red Caps and hinkypunks.

00:00:33.943 --> 00:00:34.901
We're not meant
to start

00:00:34.944 --> 00:00:36.511
nocturnal beasts
for weeks.

00:00:36.554 --> 00:00:37.642
Quiet.

00:00:37.686 --> 00:00:38.513
RON:
When did she come in?

00:00:38.556 --> 00:00:40.254
Did you see her come in?

00:00:40.297 --> 00:00:41.864
Now...

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:44.780
which one of you can tell me
the difference between

00:00:44.824 --> 00:00:46.826
an Animagus and a werewolf?

00:00:47.827 --> 00:00:49.654
No one?

00:00:49.698 --> 00:00:51.744
How disappointing.

00:00:51.787 --> 00:00:53.528
HERMIONE:
Please, sir.

00:00:53.571 --> 00:00:57.010
An Animagus is a wizard who
elects to turn into an animal.

00:00:57.053 --> 00:00:58.402
A werewolf has no choice.

00:00:58.446 --> 00:01:00.535
With each full moon,
when he transforms,

00:01:00.578 --> 00:01:01.971
he no longer
remembers who he is.

00:01:02.015 --> 00:01:04.452
He'd kill his best friend
if he crossed his path.

00:01:04.495 --> 00:01:06.497
Furthermore,
the werewolf only responds

00:01:06.541 --> 00:01:07.847
to the call of its own kind.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:09.805
[ howls][ chuckles]

00:01:09.849 --> 00:01:10.719
Thank you,

00:01:10.763 --> 00:01:12.025
Mr. Malfoy.

00:01:12.068 --> 00:01:13.417
That is the second time

00:01:13.461 --> 00:01:14.723
you have spoken
out of turn, Miss Granger.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:17.117
Are you incapable of
restraining yourself

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.379
or do you take pride

00:01:18.422 --> 00:01:20.555
in being an insufferable
know-it-all?

00:01:20.598 --> 00:01:22.557
He's got a point,
you know?

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.298
Five points from Gryffindor.

00:01:24.341 --> 00:01:26.343
As an antidote
to your ignorance,

00:01:26.387 --> 00:01:28.911
and on my desk by
Monday morning,

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.044
two rolls of parchment
on the werewolf

00:01:31.087 --> 00:01:33.133
with particular
emphasis

00:01:33.176 --> 00:01:34.656
on recognizing it.

00:01:34.699 --> 00:01:35.831
Sir, it's Quidditch tomorrow.

00:01:35.875 --> 00:01:37.050
Then I suggest

00:01:37.093 --> 00:01:39.835
you take extra
care, Mr. Potter.

00:01:39.879 --> 00:01:44.666
Loss of limb will
not excuse you.

00:01:44.709 --> 00:01:49.671
Page 394.

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:51.716
The term "werewolf"

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:57.157
is a contraction of the
Anglo-Saxon word "were,"

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.160
which means "man,"
and "wolf."

00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:02.162
"Werewolf."
Man-wolf.

00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:05.861
There's several ways
to become a werewolf.

00:02:05.905 --> 00:02:07.341
They include
being given

00:02:07.384 --> 00:02:09.386
the power of
shape-shifting,

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:11.345
being bitten
by a werewolf

00:02:11.388 --> 00:02:12.825
and being born
to...

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:15.001
[ wind whistling]

00:02:15.044 --> 00:02:18.178
[ thunder rumbling]

00:02:25.794 --> 00:02:29.102
[ chanting]:
Go, go, Gryffindor!

00:02:29.145 --> 00:02:31.104
HERMIONE:
Go, Harry!

00:02:31.147 --> 00:02:34.063
Go, Harry!

00:02:37.762 --> 00:02:38.546
[ pants]

00:02:38.589 --> 00:02:40.156
[ screams]

00:02:41.592 --> 00:02:44.204
[ panting]

00:02:50.079 --> 00:02:52.473
[ rapid fluttering]

00:02:56.085 --> 00:02:58.914
[ rapid fluttering]

00:02:58.958 --> 00:03:00.481
[ thunder booms]

00:03:00.524 --> 00:03:03.049
[ grunting]

00:03:03.092 --> 00:03:07.270
[ panting]

00:03:16.976 --> 00:03:19.369
[ rapid fluttering]

00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:31.860
[ crackling]

00:03:31.904 --> 00:03:33.209
[ grunting]

00:03:33.253 --> 00:03:36.517
[ rapid fluttering]

00:03:46.005 --> 00:03:48.137
[ grunts]

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:01.020
[ wind whistling]

00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:14.468
[ distorted whooshing]

